    土 | tǔ | soil; native; local
    坊 | fāng | neighborhood; local quarter
    乡 | xiāng | countryside; native place

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 当地 designates the specific geographical locality under discussion, often contrasted with foreign, distant, or national levels.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 当地 vs. 本地 | běndì | 本地 emphasizes 'this local place' from the speaker's own perspective ('我是本地人' I am a local), while 当地 is objective third-person referring to the place where events occur ('当地居民').
    2 | 当地 vs. 地方 | dìfang | 地方 is a broad general noun meaning any physical place or region, or provincial authorities as opposed to central government ('中央与地方').
    3 | 当地 vs. 本土 | běntǔ | 本土 refers to the homeland or mainland territory of a nation as opposed to overseas colonies ('本土作战', '本土品牌').

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 跨国企业在海外开展投资建设时，必须高度重视与当地社会的良性互动。主动招募培训当地劳动力、积极参与当地教育医疗公益事业，不仅能够有效化解文化摩擦与隔阂，更能为企业的长期稳健经营赢得深厚的民间土壤。 | Kuàguó qǐyè zài hǎiwài kāizhǎn tóuzī jiànshè shí, bìxū gāodù zhòngshì yǔ dāngdì shèhuì de liángxìng hùdòng. Zhǔdòng zhāomù péixùn dāngdì láodònglì, jījí cānyù dāngdì jiàoyù yīliáo gōngyì shìyè, bùjǐn nénggòu yǒuxiào huàjiě wénhuà mócā yǔ géhé, gèng néng wèi qǐyè de chángqī wěnjiàn jīngyíng yíngdé shēnhòu de mínjiān tǔrǎng. | When investing overseas, multinationals must foster healthy interaction with the local community. Recruiting and training local labor and participating in education charity smooths cultural frictions, cultivating popular goodwill for corporate longevity. | Al invertir en el exterior, las multinacionales deben estrechar lazos con la sociedad local. Contratar mano de obra autóctona e invertir en educación suaviza fricciones culturales ganándose el aprecio de la comunidad.
  #2 | 漫步在云南边陲的古老村寨中，扑面而来的是极其淳朴浓郁的当地民族风情。村民们身着五彩斑斓的手工刺绣服饰，热情地邀请远道而来的中外游客品尝当地特制的竹筒饭与山泉香茗，在欢歌笑语中体验天人合一的原生态民俗文化。 | Mànbù zài Yúnnán biānchuí de gǔlǎo cūnzhài zhōng, pūmiàn'érlái de shì jíqí chúnpǔ nóngyù de dāngdì mínzú fēngqíng. Cūnmínmen shēnzhe wǔcǎi-bānlán de shǒugōng cìxiù fúshì, rèqíng de yāoqǐng yuǎndào'érlái de zhōng-wài yóukè pǐncháng dāngdì tèzhì de zhútǒngfàn yǔ shānquán xiāngmíng, zài huāngē-xiàoyǔ zhōng tǐyàn tiānrén-héyī de yuánshēngtài mínsú wénhuà. | Strolling through ancient Yunnan border villages, visitors are greeted by rustic local ethnic charm. Villagers in colorful embroidered attire invite guests to taste local bamboo rice and mountain tea, sharing authentic folklore in song and laughter. | Al pasear por aldeas fronterizas de Yunnan, el viajero se sumerge en el rico tipismo local. Vestidos con bordados multicolores, los aldeanos convidan a degustar arroz en bambú y té de manantial compartiendo cantos y danzas ancestrales.
